{"id":"int-85ef5e3fc83e2f59d384ea9f295eb35a","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-25T02:24:45.363443Z","actor":"dkoosis@gmail.com","issue_id":"ferret-ubl","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"park: top-40 corpus-candidates run (3867 sessions, 263 shapes) shows near-variant fragmentation is real (~10/40 rows are eyeball-mergeable lintbrush-reviewer shapes differing by one shell tool, e.g. Read+Write+sh:ls+sh:mkdir+sh:rg vs +sh:test vs +sh:fd) but each is low-count (sessions=2-4) and spot-merges by eye in under 2 minutes, and corpus_candidates.go's own header already assigns that merge to the downstream analyst ('the analyst merges shapes that share an intent') — cluster.go would duplicate a job the architecture already delegates, with real false-merge risk; revisit once ferret-567.6 (LLM extract-assign-combine prior art) lands."}}
{"id":"int-0f31a3d49aec3856729898ad5464ee35","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-25T02:28:23.610089Z","actor":"dkoosis@gmail.com","issue_id":"ferret-567.4","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"adopt (gated secondary signal, not a burn-sort replacement): on the real ~/.claude/projects corpus (3,867 transcripts, 32 report-default findings, 272 labeled streams / 202 success+70 fail base rate), odds-ratio-vs-outcome put 5 of its top-10 |OR-1| motifs outside burn's top-10 -- e.g. ScheduleWakeup,prompt (burnRank 31/32, a=5/b=0 host streams, OR=3.93) and a 5-step git-workflow motif burn ranks 30th yet shows a 36% fail rate vs the 25% corpus base (OR=0.58, the actionable fail-correlated direction burn cannot see). But 3/32 motifs had zero labeled host streams and still produced a spurious nonzero |OR-1| from Laplace smoothing alone, so any fold-in needs a min-support gate -- filed ferret-qus for the actual implementation."}}
